The model, VAE, packing, flow-matching losses, fused optimizer, EMA and solvers
retain native implementations. The native attention frontend inherits PyTorch
deterministic mode, as validated before migration. OmniMoTModel has a mechanical
deferred-construction boundary so the VeOmni trainer controls sharding.

The native trainer module is retained because native configuration types import
it. VeOmni never instantiates it or delegates its update loop to it. Legacy robot
datasets, deployment/simulator code, checkpoints and machine environments are
excluded. The recipe owns the 0824 geometry/normalization helpers extracted from
Qwen3-PI; it does not import that policy.
